    <text><list><item>Persistent bloating with tightness of her clothes, feeling full after a few bites, a dull lower abdominal and pelvic ache, and passing urine more often, on most days for about four weeks, in a woman of 39: the ovarian cancer symptom index is positive. Examination: a distended abdomen with shifting dullness and a firm, fixed, irregular mass in the right adnexa. Suspected ovarian cancer; transvaginal ultrasound, CT, CA-125 and gynecologic oncology review booked within the week: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Family history of ovarian cancer in three relatives (her grandmother, an aunt, and a cousin) in a woman of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry; no genetic testing in the family is known: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

