    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Urgent gynecologic oncology consultation for a suspected ovarian cancer, before any surgery, to confirm the diagnosis and plan primary treatment. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Ovarian Cancer/Fallopian Tube Cancer/Primary Peritoneal Cancer, Version 4.2026 (2026); Committee Opinion No. 716: The Role of the Obstetrician-Gynecologist in the Early Detection of Epithelial Ovarian Cancer in Women at Average Risk (2017) [S]</item><item>At the first visit: the ovarian cancer symptom index, an abdominal and pelvic examination, CA-125 with CEA, blood count and chemistry, and a urine pregnancy test; transvaginal ultrasound and CT of the chest, abdomen and pelvis within the week, and image-guided biopsy if the scan shows disease outside the pelvis. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Ovarian Cancer/Fallopian Tube Cancer/Primary Peritoneal Cancer, Version 4.2026 (2026); Goff BA, et al. Development of an ovarian cancer symptom index: possibilities for earlier detection. Cancer 2007;109(2):221-227 (2007); Committee Opinion No. 716: The Role of the Obstetrician-Gynecologist in the Early Detection of Epithelial Ovarian Cancer in Women at Average Risk (2017) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
